20260905 220001.160 INFO             PET1     ESMX_Driver: index= 227                           MPIR_CVAR_ABORT_ON_LEAKED_HANDLES : If true, MPI will call MPI_Abort at MPI_Finalize if any MPI object handles have been leaked.  For example, if MPI_Comm_dup is called without calling a corresponding MPI_Comm_free.  For uninteresting reasons, enabling this option may prevent all known object leaks from being reported.  MPICH must have been configure with "--enable-g=handlealloc" or better in order for this functionality to work.
